    "created_at": "2025-06-02T19:41:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-02T19:41:48Z",
    "body": "> I think this looks good, it would certainly solve the issue. I'm a little curious if this can be simplified to \"if target is null or currentTarget is null, return null, otherwise retarget source against currentTarget\". I'm not sure of the performance cost of re-targeting twice.\r\n\r\nI think there are cases where currentTarget is null but target is not null after event dispatch, so we should continue considering target in addition to currentTarget. See the \"clearTargets\" variable here and how it only removes the target from the event in some situations (this prevents leaking nodes): https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-dispatch",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
